The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
syslog(LOG_ERR, "radius: %s: fclose(urandom_fp=%d) failed!", strerror(errno), fileno(this->urandom_fp));
syslog(LOG_ERR, "radius: %s: close(fd=%d) failed!", strerror(errno), this->fd);
syslog(LOG_ERR, "radius: %s: close(proxyfd=%d) failed!", strerror(errno), this->proxyfd);
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the code attempts to log the file descriptor values using `fileno()` and the direct file descriptor variables after the streams have been closed. When a stream is closed, `fileno()` returns -1, leading to misleading log messages that are not helpful for debugging.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
fd = fileno(this->urandom_fp);
syslog(LOG_ERR, "radius: %s: fclose(urandom_fp=%d) failed!", strerror(errno), fd);
fd = this->fd;
syslog(LOG_ERR, "radius: %s: close(fd=%d) failed!", strerror(errno), fd);
fd = this->proxyfd;
syslog(LOG_ERR, "radius: %s: close(proxyfd=%d) failed!", strerror(errno), fd);
```
Reason:
The fix involves storing the file descriptor values in a variable (`fd`) before closing the streams or file descriptors. This ensures that the correct values are logged even after the streams or file descriptors have been closed, thus providing accurate and helpful debugging information.

